+<!-- CARROT:REVIEW reviewed-for="8d9d0e14be4c9f0823d70c20defc78e0af682e9fa247d0b5b4e93de309b1fbbd" reviewed-at="2026-10-31T00:00:00Z" -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Selects how many gap levels the button cycles through. Lower counts restrict the selected TF levels; higher counts include more levels while preserving stored time values.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+On c3-pht-porter, short-tap the comma 3 GAP number or bars for descending selection. Openpilot longitudinal control respects this count; Porter conventional cruise uses 4→3→2→1→4.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Screen selection retains common/dedicated Porter GAP mode and does not directly transmit a cruise button. Holds and drags do not change the level.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
